WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.550
Mandate Layer gives an AI agent a trading mandate, and a contract on Base checks every order against it.

00:00:08.782 --> 00:00:17.082
It is a separate deployment of the PepeFi codebase, built for the Colosseum hackathon's Base track, on the Base Sepolia testnet.

00:00:19.743 --> 00:00:25.393
Agent Mode needs no wallet; it reads what the agent did straight from Base Sepolia.

00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:28.183
The agent can only trade inside its caps.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:34.790
This button runs a read-only simulation: margin 80 against a cap of 50.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.730
Nothing is sent, and the contract itself rejects it.

00:00:40.011 --> 00:00:43.831
An asset outside the session's allow-list is rejected too.

00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:47.981
The green check means the guard held; neither order was placed.

00:00:49.204 --> 00:00:51.428
Each session is a hard limit.

00:00:51.428 --> 00:00:55.644
Session 3 is active; the others are revoked or expired.

00:00:56.888 --> 00:01:04.348
The agent paid for its signals in test USDC over x402: four payments, each one on chain.

00:01:05.592 --> 00:01:10.028
In a recorded run, a Base Spend Permission allows 100 a day.

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:15.352
A second top-up would have made 110, so Coinbase's contract reverted it.

00:01:16.598 --> 00:01:26.198
Rejected orders emit no events, so this run was recorded: an over-cap order and one sent after revocation both reverted on chain.
